  "notes": "Source: Aviation Institute of Maintenance Fall 2023 Catalog, Vol. 12 (official PDF, aviationmaintenance.edu), 'Aviation Maintenance Technician' program page (p. 35-36). Hand-transcribed 2026-10-01. The catalog organizes this program as 17 sequential 120-clock-hour blocks (BLK 01-17); students progress through blocks in numbered order (the school's block/modular calendar and attendance policy treat each block as the instructional term). Each block is seeded here as one term, in the catalog's own listed order - no sequence was invented. Program: 91 weeks/21 months, 78 credit hours (*78 TOTAL in catalog), 2,040 clock hours. FAA Part 147 program; prepares for FAA Airframe and Powerplant (A&P) Mechanic certification, ending with the AMT Capstone. Offered at the Atlanta, GA Metro Area campus per the catalog's 'Programs & Courses by Campus' (p. 32).",
